Suggested fixes
  1. Menus do not depend on hover [hover-only-menus, weight 3]
     Expose submenus through a <button aria-expanded> toggle, or render submenu links in the
     page (footer sitemap) so they are reachable without hover.
  2. A sitemap is published [sitemap, weight 3]
     Publish /sitemap.xml and reference it with a Sitemap: line in robots.txt.
  3. Structured data (JSON-LD) describes the page [structured-data, weight 3]
     Add JSON-LD for Organization/WebSite on the home page and Product/Offer, FAQPage,
     ContactPoint or BreadcrumbList on inner pages.
  4. Interactive controls have accessible names [control-accessible-name, weight 10]
     Give every button, link and form control a visible text label or an
     aria-label/aria-labelledby. For icon buttons use aria-label; for inputs use <label for>.
  5. Clickable elements are real controls, not generic elements [fake-interactive-elements, weight 7]
     Use <button> or <a href> for actions and navigation. If a custom element must stay, add
     role="button", tabindex="0", a name and keyboard handlers.
  6. Navigation links are named and resolvable [navigation-links-usable, weight 7]
     Use real URLs in href for navigation items; name every nav link; if JavaScript handles
     navigation, keep a working href as fallback.
  7. llms.txt is published and well-formed [llms-txt, weight 3]
     Publish /llms.txt with an H1, a one-paragraph blockquote and H2 sections of markdown links
     to the most useful pages.
  8. Site search is exposed [search-available, weight 1]
     Expose search as <form role="search"> with a labelled <input type="search">, and declare a
     SearchAction in WebSite JSON-LD.

